% Declarations: pairwise distinctness of the consent states.
%
% DPV defines each state separately, in a definition of its own, and
% does not say in RDF that the states are distinct.  The declarations
% rest on the definitions, and a verdict resting on an instance of
% them is withdrawable by abandoning the declarations.
%
% Distinctness, not disjointness: one state may lie below another and
% still be a different state.  Disjointness is a different
% declaration, DPV-consent-definitional.ax.
%
% The declarations are stated here and instantiated by the problems.
% A problem naming two of the states below carries the inequation
% between them as a bg_dist_ statement.
%
% States: 13
% Pairs : 78
%
% ConsentExpired, ConsentGiven, ConsentInvalidated, ConsentRefused, ConsentRequestDeferred, ConsentRequested
% ConsentRevoked, ConsentStatus, ConsentStatusInvalidForProcessing, ConsentStatusValidForProcessing, ConsentUnknown, ConsentWithdrawn
% RenewedConsentGiven
